From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 22:41:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05380/11362] [outer-loop] revert Claude quota-conserve
 routing; fix a real false positive found in the process

Operator: 'the claude quota reset today, we should move the conductor's
planner etc back to claude.'

Removed ~/.config/systemd/user/carnot-conductor.service.d/50-claude-quota-
conserve-20260630.conf, daemon-reload + restart carnot-conductor.service.
Verified: AGENT_TYPE_PLANNER/RETRO=claude, AGENT_MODEL_PLANNER/RETRO=
claude-opus-4-8, AGENT_TYPE_AUDIT unset (falls back to its own claude
default). Standing experiment routing (codex/gpt-5.5,
CODEX_FORCE_EXPERIMENTS=1) unaffected -- a separate, permanent drop-in.

While verifying, found the conductor stuck 43 consecutive activation
refusals since 01:08 UTC (1.5+ hours, no self-heal possible -- the
conductor only regenerates research-roadmap-next.yaml when the file is
ABSENT, never when it repeatedly fails to activate) on milestone .471,
generated by the pre-revert codex planner. One of its 4 violations was a
genuine bug in yesterday's BLOCKED_PATTERN_MATCHED addition: a recurring
per-milestone hygiene task (exp5135-v471-source-scope-audit, whose JOB is
to verify no task reruns retired scopes) got HARD-blocked for legitimately
MENTIONING a retired scope name while auditing for it. Confirmed this
is a real recurring task shape (not a one-off) via its .470 predecessor,
python/carnot/experiment_5123_v470_source_scope_audit.py.

Added a narrow, id/title-pattern-based exemption for source-scope-audit
tasks specifically (not a broad carve-out) plus a regression test
confirming a non-audit task with the same phrase is still correctly
blocked. 2 new tests (8 total, all passing).

The remaining 3 violations in .471's stuck roadmap are genuine, pre-existing
catches (2 doomed-rerun scope-matches, 1 well-known KV260 /dev/mmcblk
precondition bug) -- unrelated to this fix, reported to the operator
separately rather than acted on unilaterally.

